What is SpringBoot ..?

Spring Boot is a Java framework that helps you build stand-alone, production-ready applications very quickly,
without writing a lot of configuration.

Main points about Spring Boot:

- No XML configuration needed (almost everything is done with annotations).
- Embedded servers (Tomcat, Jetty, etc.) — no need to deploy separately.
- Auto-configuration — it guesses and sets up most things for you.
- Production-ready features like health checks, metrics, etc.
- Easy to create REST APIs, web apps, or microservices.



** Internal Working of @SpringBootApplication  Annotation
---> It is combination of three annotations
1] @configuration
2] @EnableAutoConfiguration
3] @ComponentScan --- It will scan The classes which marked as @Component @Service etc.
