REST-API In springBoot.
REST- Representational State Transfer.

Controllers :- Special type of components which handles http requests.

Difference between @Controller and @RestController
@Controller :-
   - Used to build web applications (like returning HTML pages).
   - Returns views (like JSP, Thymeleaf templates) after processing data.
   - Needs @ResponseBody if you want to return JSON or data instead of a view.
   -
@RestController [ @Controller + @ResponseBody ]
   - Used to build REST APIs (returning JSON or XML).
   - Directly returns data (usually JSON) to the client.
   - Automatically adds @ResponseBody to all methods — no extra annotation needed.


   In short:
   @Controller = for web pages (HTML/Thymeleaf etc.).

   @RestController = for APIs (JSON/XML responses).

Example :-

   @Controller
   public class HomeController {
       @GetMapping("/home")
       public String homePage() {
           return "home"; // looks for a file like home.html or home.jsp
       }
   }

@RestController
public class ApiController {
    @GetMapping("/api/home")
    public String homeApi() {
        return "Hello from API"; // directly returns "Hello from API" as plain text or JSON
    }
}

